<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    (kuna) `option msvcstackguard` (P7 edge-virtualization, default OFF), the
    Windows sibling of `stackguard`.  GH-468 finding 3.

    MSVC's /GS scrambles a global cookie with the stack pointer at entry and
    hands the unscrambled value to a checker at every exit:

        100000  sub  rsp,0x48
        100004  mov  rax,[rip+0xff5]     ; __security_cookie @ 0x101000
        10000b  xor  rax,rsp             ; cookie ^ SP
        10000e  mov  [rsp+0x38],rax
        ...
        100028  mov  rdi,[rsp+0x38]
        10002d  xor  rdi,rsp             ; (cookie ^ SP) ^ SP  ==  cookie
        100034  call 100050              ; __security_check_cookie
        100039  mov  eax,[rsp+0x2c]
        10003d  add  rsp,0x48
        100041  ret

    The compare lives inside the callee (0x100050: `cmp rdi,[cookie] / jne
    __fastfail`), so the guarded function contains no CBRANCH, no fs:0x28 load
    and no failure edge.  The glibc matcher `stackguard` runs cannot see any of
    it, and `option stackguard on|off` is byte-identical here.

    The callee is deliberately left UNNAMED (there is no `<symbol>` for it) so
    the test pins the claim that recognition is shape-only: the trigger is the
    CALL argument computed as `(K ^ SP) ^ SP` with both stack-pointer references
    at the same frame offset, which is what makes the two XORs cancel.  A
    stripped PE has no `__security_check_cookie` symbol.

    The cookie chunk at 0x101000 is deliberately NOT readonly: MSVC's
    __security_cookie lives in writable data, and a readonly one would fold to a
    constant.

    P0 assertion: `option msvcstackguard on|off`.
    Pass 1 (default, off) is the bug: both /GS lines and the checker call
      survive (assertions #1, #2).
    Pass 2 (on) is the fix: neither survives, and the function is the one
      statement it actually computes (assertion #3, emitted by both passes).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
4883ec48488b05f50f00004831e04889442438897c2430488d542410c70241414141
8b4424300302488b7c24384831e78944242ce8170000008b44242c4883c448c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100050" readonly="true">
483b3da90f00007501c3bf02000000cd29
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x101000">
32a2df2d992b0000
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="guarded"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option msvcstackguard off</com>
  <com>lo fu guarded</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option msvcstackguard on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="kuna-msvcstackguard #1: the entry-side cookie scramble is emitted only with the option off" min="1" max="1">dat_101000 \^</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="kuna-msvcstackguard #2: the checker call is emitted only with the option off" min="1" max="1">sub_100050\(</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="kuna-msvcstackguard #3: the computation the function actually performs survives both passes" min="2" max="2">a0 \+ 0x41414141</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
